name: Link Analysis trade showcase
tagline: "A seeded trade-based money-laundering Link Analysis demo - over-invoicing between two companies that share a director, six containers shipped round a circle of three companies, letters of credit paid on bills of lading naming a vessel that was elsewhere, and six new importers at one formation-agent address paying one exporter, planted among 2 500 companies, 12 000 trades and 300 vessels with benign look-alikes"
description: "The trade-finance compliance Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (trade_company, director, trade, bill_of_lading, vessel_position, price_reference, trade_payment; register snapshots and 12 months from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, October 2026 in data/staged; 2 500 companies, about 12 000 letters of credit and collections, 12 000 bills of lading, 300 invented vessels with a position every day, 62 real HS codes with invented reference prices and about 29 000 payments) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The trade_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via, flag) of six link kinds: traded_with, on_vessel, shipped_in, directed_by, registered_at and paid; flag marks the red flags, among them vessel_elsewhere, a bill of lading whose vessel was not in its port of loading on the B/L date (vessel_position joined on vessel and date). Four Jobs derive one Dataset per saved view. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-trade-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by TradeLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-trade-data.test.mjs): 14 shipments of integrated circuits at 3 to 8 times the reference price between a Hong Kong exporter and a UK importer that share a director; the same 6 containers shipped twice round three companies in the UAE, India and Malaysia in 4 months, the value rising each leg; 5 letters of credit paid on bills of lading naming a vessel that was elsewhere; 6 importers incorporated within 2 months at one London formation-agent address, paying one Chinese exporter about 36 times what it shipped them. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a specialty supplier priced steadily over 3 times the reference, a leasing pool's boxes carried for many shippers, transhipments whose trade names the second vessel, and long-standing companies at a large business centre. Four saved views, one per story. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: trade.analyst lead, trade.manager second approver, trade.reviewer read-only, trade.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the trade_over_reference_counts and trade_over_reference_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule trade_unit_price_over_reference (a unit price over 3 times the reference between an exporter and an importer that share a director: on the shipped data it counts the 14 over-invoiced trades of the one related pair, out of 42 trades over 3 times the reference; the specialty supplier's 28 are not counted; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-trade.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only; every company, person, vessel, port and container is invented."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:globe-alt
contents[7]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (register snapshots, 12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "trade_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, red-flag column)", "Bill of lading checked against the vessel's position on the B/L date", "4 saved views, each on its own derived Dataset (over-invoicing, phantom shipment, circular trade, shell importers)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a unit price over 3x the reference between companies sharing a director (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
